Subject: [PATCH 4/5] docs(readme): correct the service-worker, provider and
 baseline claims and complete the roadmap

The root README still said the mobile app registers no service worker. The PWA
registers an offline shell worker: the production build emits dist/sw.js and
registerShellWorker registers it, with no runtime caching of daemon responses and
no push permission.

The provider FAQ was still prefixed Planned:. Rewrite it from what the crate and
the daemon's factory implement: one-click OpenAI-compatible defaults for
OpenRouter, DeepSeek, Kimi, GLM and Qwen plus a custom URL row, Anthropic's
messages API, a keyless local Ollama/LM Studio adapter, the WARSHA_LLM_* env
path and the offline fake provider, and PATH-detected coding tools whose
adapters are not yet driven. Name what does not work: no native Gemini or Azure
adapter, only their OpenAI-compatible form.

State the measured a11y baseline (188 listed, 180 passed, 8 failed on the
settings screen) instead of a bare 180 passed, and add the M10-M20 and Wave 2
roadmap rows in both languages.
